{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01601",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.5,
      "end_seconds": 3.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Sorry I'm a little late, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.36,
      "end_seconds": 8.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "yes, come in and sit down what brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.91,
      "end_seconds": 15.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got an itchy scalp."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.87,
      "end_seconds": 25.78,
      "duration_seconds": 7.91,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.71,
      "end_seconds": 31.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Erm, it's been two months, I'm fairly sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.44,
      "end_seconds": 34.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.47,
      "end_seconds": 45.53,
      "duration_seconds": 10.06,
      "text": "It usually comes with seeing tiny bugs in the hair. The seeing tiny bugs in the hair? That's been for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 47.59,
      "end_seconds": 56.53,
      "duration_seconds": 8.94,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pressure 110 over 75, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, pulse 82, temperature is 36.5 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.05,
      "end_seconds": 61.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.28,
      "end_seconds": 67.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.61,
      "end_seconds": 70.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "breathe out slowly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.85,
      "end_seconds": 94.09,
      "duration_seconds": 7.24,
      "text": "I can see live lice and small eggs close to the the roots behind the ears."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.9,
      "end_seconds": 100.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.45,
      "end_seconds": 115.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "And And what about swollen glands, fever or rash on the body?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.6,
      "end_seconds": 124.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.79,
      "text": "Actually, I haven't had swollen glands, fever or rash on the body, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.01,
      "end_seconds": 128.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.19,
      "end_seconds": 131.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.52,
      "end_seconds": 136.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.09,
      "end_seconds": 138.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.33,
      "end_seconds": 143.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.93,
      "end_seconds": 152.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.7,
      "text": "years back I got wheezing from diclofenac, so I stay away from it now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.62,
      "end_seconds": 173.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.05,
      "end_seconds": 192.28,
      "duration_seconds": 18.23,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner. No, I've never smoked in my life. I grab fast food at lunch most days. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.25,
      "end_seconds": 195.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.95,
      "end_seconds": 210.43,
      "duration_seconds": 14.48,
      "text": "Arthritis in my knees, for five years. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. I've had heart disease for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.19,
      "end_seconds": 216.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Alright, heart disease, that matches what I have here. Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.37,
      "end_seconds": 220.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Nothing, I haven't had any operations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.62,
      "end_seconds": 233.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.21,
      "end_seconds": 238.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Diclofenac, 50 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.61,
      "end_seconds": 246.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Alright, since when have you been taking it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.44,
      "end_seconds": 254.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "about about a year. I take metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.21,
      "end_seconds": 265.64,
      "duration_seconds": 10.43,
      "text": "having listened and examined, it points towards head lice. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.73,
      "end_seconds": 270.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "what are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.14,
      "end_seconds": 294.94,
      "duration_seconds": 23.8,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's head lice, and and we'll watch how it goes. I'd like you to take dimeticone lotion, 4%, once, repeat after seven days, two applications. That should help with head lice. Comb the hair with a fine comb every few days and check the family."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.25,
      "end_seconds": 306.34,
      "duration_seconds": 11.09,
      "text": "Okay, go on. If the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently. See me again if lice persist after two treatments."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.48,
      "end_seconds": 308.18,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.7,
      "end_seconds": 316.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.3,
      "end_seconds": 321.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "No, um, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.95,
      "end_seconds": 324.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "all the best"
    }
  ]
}